---
description: Close actual attempted evidence prefixes while preserving surviving ambiguity.
args:
  state: GrammarFrontier
returns: GrammarReport
---
1. Require state.pending empty and exact accounting of every original candidate/evidence pair by an attempt or an actual rejection-linked skip. Missing coverage is unresolved collection, not a surviving analysis.
2. For each original hypothesis collect its actual ordered attempts and skips. Validate that skipped evidence cites its actual first contradiction and earlier completed attempts remain retained.
3. A hypothesis with an actual contradiction stays rejected regardless of later unattempted evidence. Construct RejectedProof from that first contradiction, actual earlier attempt IDs and skipped original evidence IDs.
4. A nonrejected hypothesis survives only when every applicable usable evidence comparison completed with support. Actual unknown decisive judgments preserve status unresolved rather than rejection or arbitrary survival.
5. Do not collapse two completed survivors merely because current scenes did not ask about their differing fields. Retain their distinct source-defined choices for consequential held-out meanings and uncertain gloss repair.
6. Check every survivor/rejection ID belongs to the original inventory and every actual proof quote is original. Do not manufacture a global ideal model to replace partial candidate histories.
7. Return actual inventory, statuses, survivor IDs, attempts, rejection prefixes, skipped accounting and unresolved premises. This closes tested evidence only; it does not certify all future utterances.
